{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"carried_from":"1","checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a test that a RunRequest whose `config.model` is empty/None falls back to the runner's floor model (asserting the model handed to `_pai_model` equals `base.model`), covering `_effective_config`'s `not requested` branch.","criteria":["tests"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["src/rebar/llm/runner.py:208-211 `requested = getattr(req.config, \"model\", None)` / `if not requested or requested == base.model: return base`","runner.py:200-206 documents the branch as deliberate: 'An ABSENT or EMPTY requested model falls back to `base` rather than raising ... substituting an empty model would build a provider session for nothing and fail deep inside the SDK ... this branch exists for a direct library caller.'","tests/unit/test_llm_model_per_request.py:87-97 exercise only override (`_PER_CALL_MODEL`) and control (equal model) cases; ABSENCE: search for `model=\"\"`/`model=None` in tests/unit returned no matches, so the empty/absent path is unexercised."],"finding":"`_effective_config`'s empty/absent requested-model fallback branch (`if not requested ... return base`) is untested. The two runner tests cover only `requested == base.model` (control) and `requested != base.model` (override); no test passes a RunRequest whose `config.model` is empty/None, so the deliberately-implemented `not requested` branch — documented as the guard against building a provider session for an empty model and failing deep in the SDK — has no regression coverage.","id":"0","impact":0.3,"location":"src/rebar/llm/runner.py:208","norm_id":"nf320d3eaf9dda22a","priority":0.2143,"reason":"default-advisory","reviewer_id":"code-review-tests","reviewers":["code-review-tests"],"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7143,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_